data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"research_pack\",\"format\":\"equitylayer-research-pack/1\",\"pack_id\":\"taiwan-optical-revenue-vs-cpo-guidance\",\"revision\":\"R2\",\"parent_revision\":\"R1\",\"publisher\":\"EquityLayer Research\",\"title\":\"What Taiwan's optical suppliers report, and what they only guide on CPO\",\"view\":\"Taiwan optical revenue is rising, but none of nine suppliers checked reports CPO revenue. One laser epi supplier ties its growth to data-center shipments, and fiber attach shows only guidance on CPO so far.\",\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"stage\":\"network\",\"horizon\":\"next_disclosure\",\"as_of\":\"2026-11-10\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"freshness\":{\"freshness\":\"fresh\",\"fresh_until\":\"2026-11-17\",\"next_check_at\":\"2026-11-17\",\"next_check_reason\":\"next_release_due\"},\"access\":\"public\",\"content_sha256\":\"5e523cbcb9e2cdaf39a6f1dfd684ccfc27509925441db6c8cc24442761293ec1\",\"research_markdown\":\"## Lead\\n\\nTaiwan's optical suppliers are often read as a single CPO story, but none of the nine checked discloses a CPO revenue share in its 2025 annual report, and none states there that CPO volume shipments have started. What the filings and exchange data show is a difference in evidence. LandMark, a laser epi supplier, has revenue that its exchange note ties to data-center shipments, although not to CPO (low confidence, one issuer). On CPO, fiber attach has guidance and capital plans. Browave's annual report guides volume production for the second half of 2026; its revenue was broadly level from quarter to quarter through 3Q26, but 3Q26 was up 21.7% year on year and September up 27.4% (low confidence). FOCI's annual report plans NT$1,538,000k of equipment for an FAU line (low confidence). Monthly revenue through December can falsify a material Browave ramp if it averages below the 3Q26 level, but a rise can only be consistent with one. This edition shows exchange open data and issuer filings only, so the timing risk from NPO running ahead of or alongside CPO in scale-up is not covered here.\\n\\n## Our read\\n\\nEach read is a `hypothesis` claim with a confidence, its evidence, a test, and the variable it watches.\\n\\n1. **One laser epi supplier shows data-center revenue, and it is not shown to be CPO (low).**\\n2. **Browave's guided ramp should show by December if it is material (low).** Revenue averaging below the 3Q26 level can falsify it. A rise cannot prove it.\\n3. **FOCI's FAU line is not visible in revenue yet (low).**\\n\\nR1 also carried a risk view: that NPO stays ahead of or alongside CPO in scale-up links. Its evidence is issuer investor-relations material on rights HOLD, so R2 does not show it. See View.\\n\\n## View\\n\\nThis pack separates what suppliers have committed to from what they report. It does not rank suppliers by CPO revenue, because that number does not exist in the primary sources read.\\n\\nWhat this edition does not show, and why. Every fact here comes from TWSE or TPEx open data, or from an issuer's annual report or reviewed financial statements. AC ruled on 2026-11-10 that annual reports and reviewed statements on issuer sites are issuer filings. Press releases, call remarks, investor decks and issuer web tables are on rights HOLD, so R2 neither shows nor paraphrases them. That covers NVIDIA's CPO releases, Lumentum's results and remarks, the Marvell and Lumentum deal announcement, and Taiwan supplier investor decks, including LuxNet's NPO and CPO forecast and EZconn's ELS timing. Monthly revenue comes from the exchange tables, not from issuer web pages; July is derived from the tables and the reviewed statements. The NPO and CPO timing risk in scale-up depends on that material, so it is listed in `not_covered`. Its tracking variable, `v:lite.us.npo_cpo_statement.quarterly`, is `issuer_ir`, and its readings are withheld from public callers until the source rights are cleared.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThese are separate kinds of evidence. This pack does not establish a supply link between them or to any US program.\\n\\n- Taiwan suppliers state plans and goals for CPO in their annual reports: Browave's volume-production guidance, FOCI's FAU equipment plan, and Pcl's work on external laser sources.\\n- LandMark's exchange note ties its growth to data-center shipments, which is not the same as CPO.\\n- Monthly revenue is reported only in total, so CPO revenue is not observable today.\\n\\n## Counterevidence\\n\\nA flat month does not prove a slip, since customer timing moves. Rising revenue may come from pluggables, PON, or CATV; Browave's annual report says its fiber harness for 400G and 800G pluggables is already in stable volume shipment. LandMark's largest shipping region is China, so its growth may be unrelated to US CPO programs. At FOCI, an undefined Other line rose from NT$44,736k in 2024 to NT$313,715k in 2025, and a contract asset for integrated services first appears in 2Q26, so early FAU work could sit in lines the issuer does not label.\\n\\n## What would prove it wrong\\n\\nSee each hypothesis's test. The clearest change would be a Taiwan supplier reporting CPO revenue separately, or attributing reported revenue to CPO in a primary source.\\n\\n## Next check\\n\\nOctober 2026 monthly revenue is not yet in the open data: on 2026-11-10 both the TWSE and TPEx tables still showed September. The next check is the October tables, expected around 2026-11-17, since the retained September tables are dated between 2026-10-11 and 2026-10-17. FOCI's and Browave's 3Q26 statements are due by mid-November. The full monthly read is on 2027-01-10, after December revenue.\",\"hypotheses\":[{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"LandMark, a laser epi supplier, shows revenue its issuer ties to data-center shipments, while fiber-attach suppliers so far show only guidance on CPO. Neither is shown to be CPO revenue.\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"limitation\":\"One issuer and three months of data, with no comparison across layers. July is derived. 71.40% of LandMark's 2025 sales shipped to China, so US CPO programs may have little to do with this revenue. The closest contrary statements are in its annual report: 2025 revenue rose 82.3% as silicon photonics product shipments rose sharply (p.5), and it makes CW laser epi for silicon photonics and CPO architectures (p.76). Neither attributes revenue to CPO.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S02\",\"S40\",\"S10\",\"S06\",\"S03\"],\"method\":\"EquityLayer Research reading of the evidence claims in rests_on.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:e2513f24ecaaf2b6eb27f1774ac99bc620158ccb48f4bbae9d524b691ccce802\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":{\"falsifier\":\"A fiber-attach supplier attributes reported revenue to CPO in a primary source, two straight LandMark readings fall below NT$501,212k, or an official statement says LandMark's growth is not data center.\",\"due\":\"2027-01-10\"},\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":\"low\",\"rests_on\":[\"sha256:06edfee94b515c164884835c41104b2fb42f2467ee70fbce26a1fd901dcaf4b5\",\"sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f\",\"sha256:6abd5f400c5dae46f11d6f45a98d70454d4cd538dab0bce871a2ca06ff4d2a80\",\"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f\",\"sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a\"],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":\"core\",\"state\":\"forming\",\"common_reading\":{\"text\":\"Laser epi growth is read as CPO revenue.\",\"basis\":\"ours\",\"fact\":null},\"angle\":\"LandMark's revenue growth is real, and its exchange note ties it to data-center shipments. No primary source here ties it to CPO.\",\"mechanism\":[{\"step\":\"LandMark's exchange note attributes its growth to data-center product shipments.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:06edfee94b515c164884835c41104b2fb42f2467ee70fbce26a1fd901dcaf4b5\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"Its revenue rose each month of 3Q26.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"71.40% of its 2025 sales shipped to China, so a link to US CPO programs is not shown.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:6abd5f400c5dae46f11d6f45a98d70454d4cd538dab0bce871a2ca06ff4d2a80\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"On CPO, fiber-attach suppliers state plans, not attributed revenue.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f\",\"sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a\"],\"reasoning\":false}],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[{\"variable\":\"v:3081.two.revenue.monthly\",\"baseline\":{\"period\":\"2026-09\"},\"how_to_read\":[{\"if\":\">= 540492\",\"means\":\"strengthens\",\"say\":\"The data-center lift continues. Check that the note still cites data center.\"},{\"if\":\"501212..540492\",\"means\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"say\":\"Inside the 3Q26 range.\"},{\"if\":\"< 501212\",\"means\":\"weakens\",\"say\":\"Below the 3Q26 range, so this read needs review.\"}]}],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"Browave's guided second-half 2026 start of CPO volume production will show as a step-up in monthly revenue by December 2026 if the ramp is material to the company.\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"limitation\":\"A rise only means consistent with a ramp, because other product lines also move revenue. Revenue below the 3Q26 average can falsify a material ramp; a rise cannot prove one.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S06\",\"S07\",\"S02\"],\"method\":\"EquityLayer Research reading of the evidence claims in rests_on.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:5769684aca00f6330cc8f0f5b2b044300b80d7d810a233b48b4f8fbb15664ae8\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":{\"falsifier\":\"Revenue averages below NT$219,137k a month from October to December 2026 with no issuer statement on timing.\",\"due\":\"2027-01-10\"},\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":\"low\",\"rests_on\":[\"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f\",\"sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda\"],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":\"core\",\"state\":\"forming\",\"common_reading\":{\"text\":\"Guidance on CPO volume production is read as CPO revenue now.\",\"basis\":\"ours\",\"fact\":null},\"angle\":\"It separates guidance on CPO from reported revenue.\",\"mechanism\":[{\"step\":\"The 2025 annual report guides CPO volume production for the second half of 2026.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"Revenue was broadly level from quarter to quarter in 2026, but 3Q26 was up 21.7% year on year and September up 27.4% year on year.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"A material ramp must lift total revenue above the recent range.\",\"facts\":[],\"reasoning\":true}],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[{\"variable\":\"v:3163.two.revenue.monthly\",\"baseline\":{\"period\":\"2026-09\"},\"how_to_read\":[{\"if\":\">= 242257\",\"means\":\"strengthens\",\"say\":\"Consistent with a ramp, but it does not prove CPO.\"},{\"if\":\"219137..242257\",\"means\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"say\":\"Inside the recent range. Read the next month.\"},{\"if\":\"< 219137\",\"means\":\"weakens\",\"say\":\"Below the 3Q26 average during the guided window.\"}]}],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI's FAU line cannot yet be seen in its reported revenue, and legacy lines moving against it dominate the total.\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"limitation\":\"Monthly revenue cannot separate FAU, so a rise cannot confirm or refute this. The capex comparison uses different perimeters. The annual report expects the line to reach mass production in 2026, an undefined Other line grew sevenfold in 2025, and a contract asset for integrated services first appears in 2Q26, so early FAU work could sit in lines the issuer does not label.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S03\",\"S04\",\"S02\"],\"method\":\"EquityLayer Research reading of the evidence claims in rests_on.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:b8206f96ce1c43c54ff50604cf7810819c0f591e409aea712668309b5d5aca94\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":{\"falsifier\":\"An issuer document states an FAU shipment start and share, or a 3Q26 report shows a separate silicon photonics line.\",\"due\":\"2027-01-10\"},\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":\"low\",\"rests_on\":[\"sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a\",\"sha256:c8bd9c5513b51147e8cd2b3383cd8863cf1aaa6115d7263959d7247ec7bbdf7b\",\"sha256:219601d8078b02876e5c4983d484e3ee7d1e65202b9a90300a637dc5f16f3427\",\"sha256:1c60c1ec4d83ef31bbc4408dec87fa35252c91ea72324d8a5281f522ea626576\",\"sha256:6c1217940e7f8efa26cf42f8bff0073a7ead2f75bee33ab9e8a9dae268abd004\",\"sha256:ba2b027d108abbf872b0a03a6bdad2ef9726052b7a669a34aee82890fd73eb7f\"],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":\"supporting\",\"state\":\"forming\",\"common_reading\":{\"text\":\"FOCI's FAU shipments are read as on schedule from 3Q26.\",\"basis\":\"ours\",\"fact\":null},\"angle\":\"The capex plan is primary, the shipment claim is not, and 1H cash spending trails the plan.\",\"mechanism\":[{\"step\":\"The capital plan funds a silicon photonics FAU line.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"1H cash spending trails the planned amount.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:c8bd9c5513b51147e8cd2b3383cd8863cf1aaa6115d7263959d7247ec7bbdf7b\"],\"reasoning\":false},{\"step\":\"Americas revenue halved in 2Q26, and one customer was 70.16% in 2025.\",\"facts\":[\"sha256:1c60c1ec4d83ef31bbc4408dec87fa35252c91ea72324d8a5281f522ea626576\",\"sha256:219601d8078b02876e5c4983d484e3ee7d1e65202b9a90300a637dc5f16f3427\"],\"reasoning\":false}],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[{\"variable\":\"v:3363.two.revenue.monthly\",\"baseline\":{\"period\":\"2026-09\"},\"how_to_read\":[{\"if\":\">= 224257\",\"means\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"say\":\"Revenue is rising, but it could be FAU or a legacy recovery.\"},{\"if\":\"199861..224257\",\"means\":\"no_material_change\",\"say\":\"Inside the recent range.\"},{\"if\":\"< 199861\",\"means\":\"strengthens\",\"say\":\"No ramp is visible at the company level.\"}]}],\"binding_constraint\":null}],\"latest_edition\":{\"edition\":\"R2\",\"since\":\"R1\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"events\":[],\"variables\":[],\"views\":[{\"view\":\"sha256:e2513f24ecaaf2b6eb27f1774ac99bc620158ccb48f4bbae9d524b691ccce802\",\"move\":\"added\",\"why\":\"R1's LandMark and fiber-attach view, with the sequence limb, the Lumentum step and the value-chain gain removed; July is derived from the exchange table.\"},{\"view\":\"sha256:5769684aca00f6330cc8f0f5b2b044300b80d7d810a233b48b4f8fbb15664ae8\",\"move\":\"added\",\"why\":\"R1's Browave view, now on the annual report's guidance with year-on-year context; the NVIDIA listing is no longer cited.\"},{\"view\":\"sha256:b8206f96ce1c43c54ff50604cf7810819c0f591e409aea712668309b5d5aca94\",\"move\":\"added\",\"why\":\"R1's FOCI view, with the Other line, the 2026 mass-production plan and the 2Q26 contract asset in its limitation.\"},{\"view\":\"sha256:1311a646b9dba8963b495e0ada306d6246a7cc2e4cffa960cce21c17b9b66a6f\",\"move\":\"retired\",\"why\":\"Restated in R2 as a new view: sources moved to exchange open data and issuer filings.\"},{\"view\":\"sha256:5c310787d9a1e3356885fd3f8be55dc2f4155a9d58af623b0bd921d54c1cb027\",\"move\":\"retired\",\"why\":\"Restated in R2 as a new view: sources moved to exchange open data and issuer filings.\"},{\"view\":\"sha256:8ac646899ee49586c53a4f2f573841168997a26f9fdde300976795ab70cb05cf\",\"move\":\"retired\",\"why\":\"Restated in R2 as a new view: sources moved to exchange open data and issuer filings.\"},{\"view\":\"sha256:ebaaea35f721fddcd9a1b938596cfef209b9314952e84aa5965848d352599642\",\"move\":\"retired\",\"why\":\"The NPO and CPO scale-up risk rests on issuer IR material on rights HOLD, so R2 lists it under not_covered instead of showing it.\"}],\"facts\":{\"added\":[\"sha256:ba2b027d108abbf872b0a03a6bdad2ef9726052b7a669a34aee82890fd73eb7f\"],\"revised\":[\"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f\",\"sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda\",\"sha256:6c1217940e7f8efa26cf42f8bff0073a7ead2f75bee33ab9e8a9dae268abd004\",\"sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f\",\"sha256:14a1e85210b602078640a8148342940b732a392786688eb408a4fd2c50edfa92\",\"sha256:0c0d0bff006c8d847d0238314846bbbfc2196d8b1375e95c728a2fd01fdb8ed4\"]},\"next\":{\"what\":\"October 2026 monthly revenue in the TWSE and TPEx open-data tables\",\"at\":\"2026-11-17\"}},\"theme_id\":\"optical_cpo\",\"thesis_ids\":[\"el-optical-cpo-guidance-to-revenue\"],\"not_covered\":[\"CPO revenue by supplier because none of the nine reports it\",\"Customer identities behind coded customers\",\"Whether a named Taiwan supplier ships to NVIDIA or Broadcom or a hyperscaler under contract\",\"CPO and NPO unit forecasts as our own view\",\"Whether NPO runs ahead of or alongside CPO in scale-up links, because its evidence is issuer IR material on rights HOLD\",\"NVIDIA CPO releases, Lumentum results and remarks, and the Marvell and Lumentum deal, all issuer IR material on rights HOLD\",\"Taiwan supplier investor decks, including the LuxNet NPO and CPO forecast and EZconn ELS timing, on rights HOLD\",\"Issuer web tables of monthly revenue because monthly figures here come from the exchange tables\",\"Share prices and valuation\"],\"claims\":[{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"Browave's 2025 annual report, printed 2026-04-30, expects its CPO fiber harness and fiber distribution box product lines to start volume production in the second half of 2026.\",\"kind\":\"management_claim\",\"limitation\":\"A forward statement, not a shipment. The same report says its fiber harness for 400G and 800G pluggable transceivers is already in stable volume shipment.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S06\"],\"method\":\"Annual report PDF p.5 (printed p.2) for the CPO lines; PDF p.4 for the pluggable line.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"Browave revenue was NT$656,095k in 1Q26, NT$591,851k in 2Q26, and NT$657,412k in 3Q26. 3Q26 was NT$210,064k in July, NT$205,091k in August, and NT$242,257k in September, a monthly average of NT$219,137k, and up 21.7% from NT$540,352k in 3Q25. September was up 18.1% month on month and 27.4% year on year.\",\"kind\":\"derived_value\",\"limitation\":\"Mixes the exchange table with reviewed statements. Revenue was broadly level from quarter to quarter in 2026 but higher than a year earlier.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S07\",\"S02\"],\"method\":\"1Q is 1H 1,247,946 less 2Q 591,851 (statements PDF p.23). 3Q is the exchange's nine-month 1,905,358 less 1H. July is 3Q less August and September from the table. 3Q25 is the table's prior-year nine-month 1,602,747 less 1H25 1,062,395 (p.23).\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2025-07-01\",\"end\":\"2026-09-30\"},\"id\":\"sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI's annual report plans NT$1,538,000k of equipment for a silicon photonics FAU line: NT$461,400k each in 2Q26 and 3Q26, and NT$307,600k each in 4Q26 and 1Q27.\",\"kind\":\"reported_fact\",\"limitation\":\"A plan as of the annual report. Later changes were not checked.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S03\"],\"method\":\"Annual report PDF pp.67 to 68.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z\",\"revision\":\"R1\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI's cash spending on property, plant and equipment in 1H26 was NT$171,274k, or 37.1% of the NT$461,400k planned by the end of 2Q26.\",\"kind\":\"derived_value\",\"limitation\":\"All PP&E against one plan item, so this suggests a lag rather than proving one.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S04\",\"S03\"],\"method\":\"171,274/461,400. Statements PDF p.11 against the annual report schedule.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2026-01-01\",\"end\":\"2026-06-30\"},\"id\":\"sha256:c8bd9c5513b51147e8cd2b3383cd8863cf1aaa6115d7263959d7247ec7bbdf7b\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z\",\"revision\":\"R1\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI reports patch cords at 63.01% of 2025 revenue and one customer at 70.16%, with no silicon photonics or CPO revenue line.\",\"kind\":\"reported_fact\",\"limitation\":\"The customer is coded, not named. An undefined Other line rose from NT$44,736k in 2024 to NT$313,715k in 2025.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S03\"],\"method\":\"Annual report PDF pp.69 and 80.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2025-01-01\",\"end\":\"2025-12-31\"},\"id\":\"sha256:219601d8078b02876e5c4983d484e3ee7d1e65202b9a90300a637dc5f16f3427\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z\",\"revision\":\"R1\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI's Americas revenue fell to NT$225,307k in 2Q26 from NT$468,503k in 2Q25, down 51.9%. Mainland China revenue rose to NT$127,223k from NT$62,934k.\",\"kind\":\"derived_value\",\"limitation\":\"The issuer does not state the cause.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S04\"],\"method\":\"Statements PDF p.29. 225,307/468,503 less 1.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2025-04-01\",\"end\":\"2026-06-30\"},\"id\":\"sha256:1c60c1ec4d83ef31bbc4408dec87fa35252c91ea72324d8a5281f522ea626576\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z\",\"revision\":\"R1\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI's 3Q26 revenue was NT$599,582k, a monthly average of NT$199,861k: NT$170,843k in July, NT$204,482k in August, and NT$224,257k in September.\",\"kind\":\"derived_value\",\"limitation\":\"It cannot be attributed to the FAU line. July is derived.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S02\",\"S04\"],\"method\":\"Nine-month 1,410,739 in the exchange table less 1H 811,157 (statements PDF p.8). July is 3Q less August and September from the table.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2026-07-01\",\"end\":\"2026-09-30\"},\"id\":\"sha256:6c1217940e7f8efa26cf42f8bff0073a7ead2f75bee33ab9e8a9dae268abd004\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"LandMark's September 2026 note in the exchange table attributes its growth to data-center product shipments.\",\"kind\":\"management_claim\",\"limitation\":\"It does not separate CPO from pluggable silicon photonics.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S02\"],\"method\":\"The remarks column of the exchange table.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2026-09-01\",\"end\":\"2026-09-30\"},\"id\":\"sha256:06edfee94b515c164884835c41104b2fb42f2467ee70fbce26a1fd901dcaf4b5\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z\",\"revision\":\"R1\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"LandMark's 3Q26 revenue was NT$1,562,173k, rising each month: NT$501,212k in July, NT$520,469k in August, and NT$540,492k in September 2026.\",\"kind\":\"derived_value\",\"limitation\":\"July is derived: the exchange's nine-month total less the 1H26 statements, less August and September. It is NT$2k above the July figure on the issuer's own site, whose monthly figures sum to NT$2k less than the exchange's nine-month total. The cause is not determined.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S02\",\"S40\"],\"method\":\"August and September from the September exchange table. 3Q is the table's nine-month 3,687,740 less 1H26 revenue 2,125,567 (2Q26 statements PDF p.5). July is 3Q less August and September.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2026-07-01\",\"end\":\"2026-09-30\"},\"id\":\"sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"71.40% of LandMark's 2025 sales shipped to China and 21.46% to the US.\",\"kind\":\"reported_fact\",\"limitation\":\"Shipping region, not end demand.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S10\"],\"method\":\"Annual report PDF p.79.\"},\"period\":{\"start\":\"2025-01-01\",\"end\":\"2025-12-31\"},\"id\":\"sha256:6abd5f400c5dae46f11d6f45a98d70454d4cd538dab0bce871a2ca06ff4d2a80\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z\",\"revision\":\"R1\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"Pcl Technologies says it works with a leading switch chip-set maker on external laser sources (ELS) and pluggable external laser sources (ELSFP) for CPO.\",\"kind\":\"management_claim\",\"limitation\":\"No volume, revenue, or named customer.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S18\"],\"method\":\"Annual report PDF p.6.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:14a1e85210b602078640a8148342940b732a392786688eb408a4fd2c50edfa92\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"None of nine Taiwan optical suppliers, VPEC (2455), LandMark (3081), Browave (3163), FOCI (3363), Elite (3450), IET (4971), Pcl (4977), LuxNet (4979) and EZconn (6442), discloses a CPO revenue share in its 2025 annual report, and none states there that CPO volume shipments have started.\",\"kind\":\"unknown\",\"limitation\":\"A term search of the nine reports with every match read, not a cover-to-cover reading. What they state are plans and development work, such as Browave p.5, FOCI p.77 and Pcl p.6. Investor decks are not counted here, and filings available only through MOPS were not fetched. IET and EZconn, two of the nine, are linked by a share swap that IET's report describes (pp.75-76).\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S14\",\"S10\",\"S06\",\"S03\",\"S27\",\"S17\",\"S18\",\"S22\",\"S25\"],\"method\":\"Searched each report for CPO, co-packaged, 共同封裝, 共封裝 and NPO, and read every match. PDF pages with matches: VPEC none; LandMark 74, 76; Browave 4-5, 60-61, 67, 78-79; FOCI 36, 68-73, 76-77, 90-91; Elite 84; IET 76; Pcl 6, 31, 42, 44, 47-48; LuxNet 6, 74, 89-90; EZconn 8, 87.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:0c0d0bff006c8d847d0238314846bbbfc2196d8b1375e95c728a2fd01fdb8ed4\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null},{\"assertion\":{\"statement\":\"FOCI's 2025 annual report expects its silicon photonics fiber-array line to reach mass production in 2026. Its 2Q26 statements show a NT$3,877k contract asset for highly integrated service contracts at 2026-06-30, with none at the end of 2025.\",\"kind\":\"reported_fact\",\"limitation\":\"The statements do not say what the integrated service contracts cover.\"},\"provenance\":{\"source_ids\":[\"S03\",\"S04\"],\"method\":\"Annual report PDF p.77. Statements PDF p.29.\"},\"period\":null,\"id\":\"sha256:ba2b027d108abbf872b0a03a6bdad2ef9726052b7a669a34aee82890fd73eb7f\",\"publication\":{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z\",\"revision\":\"R2\"},\"test\":null,\"resolution\":{\"status\":\"Open\",\"resolved_at\":null,\"note\":null},\"confidence\":null,\"rests_on\":[],\"last_check\":null,\"role\":null,\"state\":null,\"common_reading\":null,\"angle\":null,\"mechanism\":[],\"where_value_moves\":[],\"watches\":[],\"binding_constraint\":null}],\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"S02\",\"url\":\"https://www.tpex.org.tw/openapi/v1/mopsfin_t187ap05_O\",\"publisher\":\"Taipei Exchange open data\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-10-17\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T12:57:55.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"a27fea120daa8ef4543bcbf6e31426cad2e0201111ee8d97916fbb5fce2727a6\"},{\"id\":\"S03\",\"url\":\"https://www.foci.com.tw/zh-tw/index.php?route=investor/finance_year/downloadfile&file=69fd708ac5ef4.pdf&displayname=2025AR.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"FOCI Fiber Optic\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-03-30\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:02:22.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"eb0eab0509bf3c6268bd6e3a2b6f19bb5cf15f951c3b84f894a05236766af65f\"},{\"id\":\"S04\",\"url\":\"https://www.foci.com.tw/zh-tw/index.php?route=investor/finance_quarter/downloadfile&file=6a8d424aac00d.pdf&displayname=2026Q2.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"FOCI Fiber Optic\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-08-06\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:02:19.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"b37a54105ed6cc1717babc17c2fc8c882e22741669907b3d0cc6aba42e24cc3f\"},{\"id\":\"S06\",\"url\":\"https://www.browave.com/uploads/images/%E6%B0%91%E5%9C%8B114%E5%B9%B4%E5%BA%A6%E5%B9%B4%E5%A0%B1.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"Browave\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-04-30\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:03:16.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"b05fe3defacbaca217487a9652351c56f8ed8be0522ea78acee7a8719656c6d3\"},{\"id\":\"S07\",\"url\":\"https://www.browave.com/uploads/images/2026Q2%20%E5%90%88%E4%BD%B5%E8%B2%A1%E5%8B%99%E5%A0%B1%E5%91%8A.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"Browave\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-08-06\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:03:17.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"ea4ca30a925c0dec744b59c764c96ec6eae8b27513edb3f13524245d841f6015\"},{\"id\":\"S10\",\"url\":\"https://www.lmoc.com.tw/index.php?option=module&lang=cht&task=dfile&id=390&i=1\",\"publisher\":\"LandMark Optoelectronics\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-03-31\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:04:25.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"51a5b88ab0785413998911441429ee5fd098d8a6fb5ea9ffbccc4bdef39c0feb\"},{\"id\":\"S40\",\"url\":\"https://www.lmoc.com.tw/index.php?option=module&lang=cht&task=dfile&id=396&i=1\",\"publisher\":\"LandMark Optoelectronics\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-08-12\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:33:55.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"2da0c3161904da65755e8cac9db9ec1403e25b79461d9cf2e0740fc85139bea4\"},{\"id\":\"S14\",\"url\":\"http://www.vpec.com.tw/vpec/hmanager/hmanager_c/files/fck_files/%E5%B9%B4%E5%A0%B15%E6%A0%A1(1).pdf\",\"publisher\":\"Visual Photonics Epitaxy (VPEC)\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-04-10\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:14:38.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"c994b246b4a54678ac3981c672ab495bfc9bf2493378ddcb205cfeec0218a714\"},{\"id\":\"S17\",\"url\":\"http://www.intelliepi.com/tw/doc/stockholderMeeting/2026/annualReport.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"IntelliEPI (IET)\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-05-12\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:03:19.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"5e3d1da3ccd386d1034d36b96b063184c99106c74486edb7570942ec1baa5699\"},{\"id\":\"S18\",\"url\":\"http://www.pcltech.com/file/114_ann.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"Pcl Technologies\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-05-20\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:14:36.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"7cf1ae36ae5f0a296e1ffcc907fb659ef89e07edecd2dcd1cfa2f0e65ab622c6\"},{\"id\":\"S22\",\"url\":\"https://www.luxnetcorp.com.tw/storage/architecture/page~103/page~123/114_4.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"LuxNet\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-03-31\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:06:46.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"ba6207aaa454fa444e1410e762275b6a6a8fd0c45df2375781b3a475ae1fb714\"},{\"id\":\"S25\",\"url\":\"https://www.ezconn.com/download/0326052611wf674355?open=0\",\"publisher\":\"EZconn\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-03-28\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:06:46.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"34d4ed2f4e4bcf8c1e46ba107ab5c5748d6570bfeb7c03d27bc36bbfbe96ced9\"},{\"id\":\"S27\",\"url\":\"http://www.elaser.com.tw/download/115%E8%82%A1%E6%9D%B1%E6%9C%83%E5%B9%B4%E5%A0%B1-EN-FINAL.pdf\",\"publisher\":\"Elite Advanced Laser\",\"published_at\":null,\"published_on\":\"2026-05-06\",\"publication_gap\":null,\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-11-04T13:06:26.000Z\",\"sha256\":\"afd8360f25a31eee7a82e6dff52f8d4317d807702725ed07bb25426e0deec140\"}],\"cite_as\":{\"title\":\"What Taiwan's optical suppliers report, and what they only guide on CPO\",\"publisher\":\"EquityLayer Research\",\"version\":\"R2\",\"as_of\":\"2026-11-10\",\"url\":\"https://equitylayer.io/research/packs/taiwan-optical-revenue-vs-cpo-guidance\",\"original_url\":null,\"text\":\"EquityLayer Research. \\\"What Taiwan's optical suppliers report, and what they only guide on CPO.\\\" R2, as of 2026-11-10. https://equitylayer.io/research/packs/taiwan-optical-revenue-vs-cpo-guidance\"},\"receipt_url\":\"https://equitylayer.io/research/packs/taiwan-optical-revenue-vs-cpo-guidance\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"kind":"research_pack","format":"equitylayer-research-pack/1","pack_id":"taiwan-optical-revenue-vs-cpo-guidance","revision":"R2","parent_revision":"R1","publisher":"EquityLayer Research","title":"What Taiwan's optical suppliers report, and what they only guide on CPO","view":"Taiwan optical revenue is rising, but none of nine suppliers checked reports CPO revenue. One laser epi supplier ties its growth to data-center shipments, and fiber attach shows only guidance on CPO so far.","status":"VERIFIED","stage":"network","horizon":"next_disclosure","as_of":"2026-11-10","recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","freshness":{"freshness":"fresh","fresh_until":"2026-11-17","next_check_at":"2026-11-17","next_check_reason":"next_release_due"},"access":"public","content_sha256":"5e523cbcb9e2cdaf39a6f1dfd684ccfc27509925441db6c8cc24442761293ec1","research_markdown":"## Lead\n\nTaiwan's optical suppliers are often read as a single CPO story, but none of the nine checked discloses a CPO revenue share in its 2025 annual report, and none states there that CPO volume shipments have started. What the filings and exchange data show is a difference in evidence. LandMark, a laser epi supplier, has revenue that its exchange note ties to data-center shipments, although not to CPO (low confidence, one issuer). On CPO, fiber attach has guidance and capital plans. Browave's annual report guides volume production for the second half of 2026; its revenue was broadly level from quarter to quarter through 3Q26, but 3Q26 was up 21.7% year on year and September up 27.4% (low confidence). FOCI's annual report plans NT$1,538,000k of equipment for an FAU line (low confidence). Monthly revenue through December can falsify a material Browave ramp if it averages below the 3Q26 level, but a rise can only be consistent with one. This edition shows exchange open data and issuer filings only, so the timing risk from NPO running ahead of or alongside CPO in scale-up is not covered here.\n\n## Our read\n\nEach read is a `hypothesis` claim with a confidence, its evidence, a test, and the variable it watches.\n\n1. **One laser epi supplier shows data-center revenue, and it is not shown to be CPO (low).**\n2. **Browave's guided ramp should show by December if it is material (low).** Revenue averaging below the 3Q26 level can falsify it. A rise cannot prove it.\n3. **FOCI's FAU line is not visible in revenue yet (low).**\n\nR1 also carried a risk view: that NPO stays ahead of or alongside CPO in scale-up links. Its evidence is issuer investor-relations material on rights HOLD, so R2 does not show it. See View.\n\n## View\n\nThis pack separates what suppliers have committed to from what they report. It does not rank suppliers by CPO revenue, because that number does not exist in the primary sources read.\n\nWhat this edition does not show, and why. Every fact here comes from TWSE or TPEx open data, or from an issuer's annual report or reviewed financial statements. AC ruled on 2026-11-10 that annual reports and reviewed statements on issuer sites are issuer filings. Press releases, call remarks, investor decks and issuer web tables are on rights HOLD, so R2 neither shows nor paraphrases them. That covers NVIDIA's CPO releases, Lumentum's results and remarks, the Marvell and Lumentum deal announcement, and Taiwan supplier investor decks, including LuxNet's NPO and CPO forecast and EZconn's ELS timing. Monthly revenue comes from the exchange tables, not from issuer web pages; July is derived from the tables and the reviewed statements. The NPO and CPO timing risk in scale-up depends on that material, so it is listed in `not_covered`. Its tracking variable, `v:lite.us.npo_cpo_statement.quarterly`, is `issuer_ir`, and its readings are withheld from public callers until the source rights are cleared.\n\n## Why\n\nThese are separate kinds of evidence. This pack does not establish a supply link between them or to any US program.\n\n- Taiwan suppliers state plans and goals for CPO in their annual reports: Browave's volume-production guidance, FOCI's FAU equipment plan, and Pcl's work on external laser sources.\n- LandMark's exchange note ties its growth to data-center shipments, which is not the same as CPO.\n- Monthly revenue is reported only in total, so CPO revenue is not observable today.\n\n## Counterevidence\n\nA flat month does not prove a slip, since customer timing moves. Rising revenue may come from pluggables, PON, or CATV; Browave's annual report says its fiber harness for 400G and 800G pluggables is already in stable volume shipment. LandMark's largest shipping region is China, so its growth may be unrelated to US CPO programs. At FOCI, an undefined Other line rose from NT$44,736k in 2024 to NT$313,715k in 2025, and a contract asset for integrated services first appears in 2Q26, so early FAU work could sit in lines the issuer does not label.\n\n## What would prove it wrong\n\nSee each hypothesis's test. The clearest change would be a Taiwan supplier reporting CPO revenue separately, or attributing reported revenue to CPO in a primary source.\n\n## Next check\n\nOctober 2026 monthly revenue is not yet in the open data: on 2026-11-10 both the TWSE and TPEx tables still showed September. The next check is the October tables, expected around 2026-11-17, since the retained September tables are dated between 2026-10-11 and 2026-10-17. FOCI's and Browave's 3Q26 statements are due by mid-November. The full monthly read is on 2027-01-10, after December revenue.","hypotheses":[{"assertion":{"statement":"LandMark, a laser epi supplier, shows revenue its issuer ties to data-center shipments, while fiber-attach suppliers so far show only guidance on CPO. Neither is shown to be CPO revenue.","kind":"hypothesis","limitation":"One issuer and three months of data, with no comparison across layers. July is derived. 71.40% of LandMark's 2025 sales shipped to China, so US CPO programs may have little to do with this revenue. The closest contrary statements are in its annual report: 2025 revenue rose 82.3% as silicon photonics product shipments rose sharply (p.5), and it makes CW laser epi for silicon photonics and CPO architectures (p.76). Neither attributes revenue to CPO."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S02","S40","S10","S06","S03"],"method":"EquityLayer Research reading of the evidence claims in rests_on."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:e2513f24ecaaf2b6eb27f1774ac99bc620158ccb48f4bbae9d524b691ccce802","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":{"falsifier":"A fiber-attach supplier attributes reported revenue to CPO in a primary source, two straight LandMark readings fall below NT$501,212k, or an official statement says LandMark's growth is not data center.","due":"2027-01-10"},"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":"low","rests_on":["sha256:06edfee94b515c164884835c41104b2fb42f2467ee70fbce26a1fd901dcaf4b5","sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f","sha256:6abd5f400c5dae46f11d6f45a98d70454d4cd538dab0bce871a2ca06ff4d2a80","sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f","sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a"],"last_check":null,"role":"core","state":"forming","common_reading":{"text":"Laser epi growth is read as CPO revenue.","basis":"ours","fact":null},"angle":"LandMark's revenue growth is real, and its exchange note ties it to data-center shipments. No primary source here ties it to CPO.","mechanism":[{"step":"LandMark's exchange note attributes its growth to data-center product shipments.","facts":["sha256:06edfee94b515c164884835c41104b2fb42f2467ee70fbce26a1fd901dcaf4b5"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"Its revenue rose each month of 3Q26.","facts":["sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"71.40% of its 2025 sales shipped to China, so a link to US CPO programs is not shown.","facts":["sha256:6abd5f400c5dae46f11d6f45a98d70454d4cd538dab0bce871a2ca06ff4d2a80"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"On CPO, fiber-attach suppliers state plans, not attributed revenue.","facts":["sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f","sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a"],"reasoning":false}],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[{"variable":"v:3081.two.revenue.monthly","baseline":{"period":"2026-09"},"how_to_read":[{"if":">= 540492","means":"strengthens","say":"The data-center lift continues. Check that the note still cites data center."},{"if":"501212..540492","means":"insufficient_evidence","say":"Inside the 3Q26 range."},{"if":"< 501212","means":"weakens","say":"Below the 3Q26 range, so this read needs review."}]}],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"Browave's guided second-half 2026 start of CPO volume production will show as a step-up in monthly revenue by December 2026 if the ramp is material to the company.","kind":"hypothesis","limitation":"A rise only means consistent with a ramp, because other product lines also move revenue. Revenue below the 3Q26 average can falsify a material ramp; a rise cannot prove one."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S06","S07","S02"],"method":"EquityLayer Research reading of the evidence claims in rests_on."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:5769684aca00f6330cc8f0f5b2b044300b80d7d810a233b48b4f8fbb15664ae8","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":{"falsifier":"Revenue averages below NT$219,137k a month from October to December 2026 with no issuer statement on timing.","due":"2027-01-10"},"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":"low","rests_on":["sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f","sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda"],"last_check":null,"role":"core","state":"forming","common_reading":{"text":"Guidance on CPO volume production is read as CPO revenue now.","basis":"ours","fact":null},"angle":"It separates guidance on CPO from reported revenue.","mechanism":[{"step":"The 2025 annual report guides CPO volume production for the second half of 2026.","facts":["sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"Revenue was broadly level from quarter to quarter in 2026, but 3Q26 was up 21.7% year on year and September up 27.4% year on year.","facts":["sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"A material ramp must lift total revenue above the recent range.","facts":[],"reasoning":true}],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[{"variable":"v:3163.two.revenue.monthly","baseline":{"period":"2026-09"},"how_to_read":[{"if":">= 242257","means":"strengthens","say":"Consistent with a ramp, but it does not prove CPO."},{"if":"219137..242257","means":"insufficient_evidence","say":"Inside the recent range. Read the next month."},{"if":"< 219137","means":"weakens","say":"Below the 3Q26 average during the guided window."}]}],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI's FAU line cannot yet be seen in its reported revenue, and legacy lines moving against it dominate the total.","kind":"hypothesis","limitation":"Monthly revenue cannot separate FAU, so a rise cannot confirm or refute this. The capex comparison uses different perimeters. The annual report expects the line to reach mass production in 2026, an undefined Other line grew sevenfold in 2025, and a contract asset for integrated services first appears in 2Q26, so early FAU work could sit in lines the issuer does not label."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S03","S04","S02"],"method":"EquityLayer Research reading of the evidence claims in rests_on."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:b8206f96ce1c43c54ff50604cf7810819c0f591e409aea712668309b5d5aca94","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":{"falsifier":"An issuer document states an FAU shipment start and share, or a 3Q26 report shows a separate silicon photonics line.","due":"2027-01-10"},"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":"low","rests_on":["sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a","sha256:c8bd9c5513b51147e8cd2b3383cd8863cf1aaa6115d7263959d7247ec7bbdf7b","sha256:219601d8078b02876e5c4983d484e3ee7d1e65202b9a90300a637dc5f16f3427","sha256:1c60c1ec4d83ef31bbc4408dec87fa35252c91ea72324d8a5281f522ea626576","sha256:6c1217940e7f8efa26cf42f8bff0073a7ead2f75bee33ab9e8a9dae268abd004","sha256:ba2b027d108abbf872b0a03a6bdad2ef9726052b7a669a34aee82890fd73eb7f"],"last_check":null,"role":"supporting","state":"forming","common_reading":{"text":"FOCI's FAU shipments are read as on schedule from 3Q26.","basis":"ours","fact":null},"angle":"The capex plan is primary, the shipment claim is not, and 1H cash spending trails the plan.","mechanism":[{"step":"The capital plan funds a silicon photonics FAU line.","facts":["sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"1H cash spending trails the planned amount.","facts":["sha256:c8bd9c5513b51147e8cd2b3383cd8863cf1aaa6115d7263959d7247ec7bbdf7b"],"reasoning":false},{"step":"Americas revenue halved in 2Q26, and one customer was 70.16% in 2025.","facts":["sha256:1c60c1ec4d83ef31bbc4408dec87fa35252c91ea72324d8a5281f522ea626576","sha256:219601d8078b02876e5c4983d484e3ee7d1e65202b9a90300a637dc5f16f3427"],"reasoning":false}],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[{"variable":"v:3363.two.revenue.monthly","baseline":{"period":"2026-09"},"how_to_read":[{"if":">= 224257","means":"insufficient_evidence","say":"Revenue is rising, but it could be FAU or a legacy recovery."},{"if":"199861..224257","means":"no_material_change","say":"Inside the recent range."},{"if":"< 199861","means":"strengthens","say":"No ramp is visible at the company level."}]}],"binding_constraint":null}],"latest_edition":{"edition":"R2","since":"R1","recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","events":[],"variables":[],"views":[{"view":"sha256:e2513f24ecaaf2b6eb27f1774ac99bc620158ccb48f4bbae9d524b691ccce802","move":"added","why":"R1's LandMark and fiber-attach view, with the sequence limb, the Lumentum step and the value-chain gain removed; July is derived from the exchange table."},{"view":"sha256:5769684aca00f6330cc8f0f5b2b044300b80d7d810a233b48b4f8fbb15664ae8","move":"added","why":"R1's Browave view, now on the annual report's guidance with year-on-year context; the NVIDIA listing is no longer cited."},{"view":"sha256:b8206f96ce1c43c54ff50604cf7810819c0f591e409aea712668309b5d5aca94","move":"added","why":"R1's FOCI view, with the Other line, the 2026 mass-production plan and the 2Q26 contract asset in its limitation."},{"view":"sha256:1311a646b9dba8963b495e0ada306d6246a7cc2e4cffa960cce21c17b9b66a6f","move":"retired","why":"Restated in R2 as a new view: sources moved to exchange open data and issuer filings."},{"view":"sha256:5c310787d9a1e3356885fd3f8be55dc2f4155a9d58af623b0bd921d54c1cb027","move":"retired","why":"Restated in R2 as a new view: sources moved to exchange open data and issuer filings."},{"view":"sha256:8ac646899ee49586c53a4f2f573841168997a26f9fdde300976795ab70cb05cf","move":"retired","why":"Restated in R2 as a new view: sources moved to exchange open data and issuer filings."},{"view":"sha256:ebaaea35f721fddcd9a1b938596cfef209b9314952e84aa5965848d352599642","move":"retired","why":"The NPO and CPO scale-up risk rests on issuer IR material on rights HOLD, so R2 lists it under not_covered instead of showing it."}],"facts":{"added":["sha256:ba2b027d108abbf872b0a03a6bdad2ef9726052b7a669a34aee82890fd73eb7f"],"revised":["sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f","sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda","sha256:6c1217940e7f8efa26cf42f8bff0073a7ead2f75bee33ab9e8a9dae268abd004","sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f","sha256:14a1e85210b602078640a8148342940b732a392786688eb408a4fd2c50edfa92","sha256:0c0d0bff006c8d847d0238314846bbbfc2196d8b1375e95c728a2fd01fdb8ed4"]},"next":{"what":"October 2026 monthly revenue in the TWSE and TPEx open-data tables","at":"2026-11-17"}},"theme_id":"optical_cpo","thesis_ids":["el-optical-cpo-guidance-to-revenue"],"not_covered":["CPO revenue by supplier because none of the nine reports it","Customer identities behind coded customers","Whether a named Taiwan supplier ships to NVIDIA or Broadcom or a hyperscaler under contract","CPO and NPO unit forecasts as our own view","Whether NPO runs ahead of or alongside CPO in scale-up links, because its evidence is issuer IR material on rights HOLD","NVIDIA CPO releases, Lumentum results and remarks, and the Marvell and Lumentum deal, all issuer IR material on rights HOLD","Taiwan supplier investor decks, including the LuxNet NPO and CPO forecast and EZconn ELS timing, on rights HOLD","Issuer web tables of monthly revenue because monthly figures here come from the exchange tables","Share prices and valuation"],"claims":[{"assertion":{"statement":"Browave's 2025 annual report, printed 2026-04-30, expects its CPO fiber harness and fiber distribution box product lines to start volume production in the second half of 2026.","kind":"management_claim","limitation":"A forward statement, not a shipment. The same report says its fiber harness for 400G and 800G pluggable transceivers is already in stable volume shipment."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S06"],"method":"Annual report PDF p.5 (printed p.2) for the CPO lines; PDF p.4 for the pluggable line."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:e6a50b13d8174e632f4a00fbb1494d6fbb5bec29af930554b5a08571929dfe4f","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"Browave revenue was NT$656,095k in 1Q26, NT$591,851k in 2Q26, and NT$657,412k in 3Q26. 3Q26 was NT$210,064k in July, NT$205,091k in August, and NT$242,257k in September, a monthly average of NT$219,137k, and up 21.7% from NT$540,352k in 3Q25. September was up 18.1% month on month and 27.4% year on year.","kind":"derived_value","limitation":"Mixes the exchange table with reviewed statements. Revenue was broadly level from quarter to quarter in 2026 but higher than a year earlier."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S07","S02"],"method":"1Q is 1H 1,247,946 less 2Q 591,851 (statements PDF p.23). 3Q is the exchange's nine-month 1,905,358 less 1H. July is 3Q less August and September from the table. 3Q25 is the table's prior-year nine-month 1,602,747 less 1H25 1,062,395 (p.23)."},"period":{"start":"2025-07-01","end":"2026-09-30"},"id":"sha256:725c6e0f24c1f99a31b259ed96c02abf2d667fa3912ad2c46ca6d72e6ca0ceda","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI's annual report plans NT$1,538,000k of equipment for a silicon photonics FAU line: NT$461,400k each in 2Q26 and 3Q26, and NT$307,600k each in 4Q26 and 1Q27.","kind":"reported_fact","limitation":"A plan as of the annual report. Later changes were not checked."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S03"],"method":"Annual report PDF pp.67 to 68."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:5c13b759f40f690ff742925a07ebe56790a892622feca4925915d7e159efe83a","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z","revision":"R1"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI's cash spending on property, plant and equipment in 1H26 was NT$171,274k, or 37.1% of the NT$461,400k planned by the end of 2Q26.","kind":"derived_value","limitation":"All PP&E against one plan item, so this suggests a lag rather than proving one."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S04","S03"],"method":"171,274/461,400. Statements PDF p.11 against the annual report schedule."},"period":{"start":"2026-01-01","end":"2026-06-30"},"id":"sha256:c8bd9c5513b51147e8cd2b3383cd8863cf1aaa6115d7263959d7247ec7bbdf7b","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z","revision":"R1"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI reports patch cords at 63.01% of 2025 revenue and one customer at 70.16%, with no silicon photonics or CPO revenue line.","kind":"reported_fact","limitation":"The customer is coded, not named. An undefined Other line rose from NT$44,736k in 2024 to NT$313,715k in 2025."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S03"],"method":"Annual report PDF pp.69 and 80."},"period":{"start":"2025-01-01","end":"2025-12-31"},"id":"sha256:219601d8078b02876e5c4983d484e3ee7d1e65202b9a90300a637dc5f16f3427","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z","revision":"R1"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI's Americas revenue fell to NT$225,307k in 2Q26 from NT$468,503k in 2Q25, down 51.9%. Mainland China revenue rose to NT$127,223k from NT$62,934k.","kind":"derived_value","limitation":"The issuer does not state the cause."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S04"],"method":"Statements PDF p.29. 225,307/468,503 less 1."},"period":{"start":"2025-04-01","end":"2026-06-30"},"id":"sha256:1c60c1ec4d83ef31bbc4408dec87fa35252c91ea72324d8a5281f522ea626576","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z","revision":"R1"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI's 3Q26 revenue was NT$599,582k, a monthly average of NT$199,861k: NT$170,843k in July, NT$204,482k in August, and NT$224,257k in September.","kind":"derived_value","limitation":"It cannot be attributed to the FAU line. July is derived."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S02","S04"],"method":"Nine-month 1,410,739 in the exchange table less 1H 811,157 (statements PDF p.8). July is 3Q less August and September from the table."},"period":{"start":"2026-07-01","end":"2026-09-30"},"id":"sha256:6c1217940e7f8efa26cf42f8bff0073a7ead2f75bee33ab9e8a9dae268abd004","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"LandMark's September 2026 note in the exchange table attributes its growth to data-center product shipments.","kind":"management_claim","limitation":"It does not separate CPO from pluggable silicon photonics."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S02"],"method":"The remarks column of the exchange table."},"period":{"start":"2026-09-01","end":"2026-09-30"},"id":"sha256:06edfee94b515c164884835c41104b2fb42f2467ee70fbce26a1fd901dcaf4b5","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z","revision":"R1"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"LandMark's 3Q26 revenue was NT$1,562,173k, rising each month: NT$501,212k in July, NT$520,469k in August, and NT$540,492k in September 2026.","kind":"derived_value","limitation":"July is derived: the exchange's nine-month total less the 1H26 statements, less August and September. It is NT$2k above the July figure on the issuer's own site, whose monthly figures sum to NT$2k less than the exchange's nine-month total. The cause is not determined."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S02","S40"],"method":"August and September from the September exchange table. 3Q is the table's nine-month 3,687,740 less 1H26 revenue 2,125,567 (2Q26 statements PDF p.5). July is 3Q less August and September."},"period":{"start":"2026-07-01","end":"2026-09-30"},"id":"sha256:f52de107e7e743d35e3dd36f68f9d640974ad9bf820d7323624f8eca6639af8f","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"71.40% of LandMark's 2025 sales shipped to China and 21.46% to the US.","kind":"reported_fact","limitation":"Shipping region, not end demand."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S10"],"method":"Annual report PDF p.79."},"period":{"start":"2025-01-01","end":"2025-12-31"},"id":"sha256:6abd5f400c5dae46f11d6f45a98d70454d4cd538dab0bce871a2ca06ff4d2a80","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-05T02:39:46Z","revision":"R1"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"Pcl Technologies says it works with a leading switch chip-set maker on external laser sources (ELS) and pluggable external laser sources (ELSFP) for CPO.","kind":"management_claim","limitation":"No volume, revenue, or named customer."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S18"],"method":"Annual report PDF p.6."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:14a1e85210b602078640a8148342940b732a392786688eb408a4fd2c50edfa92","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"None of nine Taiwan optical suppliers, VPEC (2455), LandMark (3081), Browave (3163), FOCI (3363), Elite (3450), IET (4971), Pcl (4977), LuxNet (4979) and EZconn (6442), discloses a CPO revenue share in its 2025 annual report, and none states there that CPO volume shipments have started.","kind":"unknown","limitation":"A term search of the nine reports with every match read, not a cover-to-cover reading. What they state are plans and development work, such as Browave p.5, FOCI p.77 and Pcl p.6. Investor decks are not counted here, and filings available only through MOPS were not fetched. IET and EZconn, two of the nine, are linked by a share swap that IET's report describes (pp.75-76)."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S14","S10","S06","S03","S27","S17","S18","S22","S25"],"method":"Searched each report for CPO, co-packaged, 共同封裝, 共封裝 and NPO, and read every match. PDF pages with matches: VPEC none; LandMark 74, 76; Browave 4-5, 60-61, 67, 78-79; FOCI 36, 68-73, 76-77, 90-91; Elite 84; IET 76; Pcl 6, 31, 42, 44, 47-48; LuxNet 6, 74, 89-90; EZconn 8, 87."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:0c0d0bff006c8d847d0238314846bbbfc2196d8b1375e95c728a2fd01fdb8ed4","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"where_value_moves":[],"watches":[],"binding_constraint":null},{"assertion":{"statement":"FOCI's 2025 annual report expects its silicon photonics fiber-array line to reach mass production in 2026. Its 2Q26 statements show a NT$3,877k contract asset for highly integrated service contracts at 2026-06-30, with none at the end of 2025.","kind":"reported_fact","limitation":"The statements do not say what the integrated service contracts cover."},"provenance":{"source_ids":["S03","S04"],"method":"Annual report PDF p.77. Statements PDF p.29."},"period":null,"id":"sha256:ba2b027d108abbf872b0a03a6bdad2ef9726052b7a669a34aee82890fd73eb7f","publication":{"recorded_at":"2026-11-10T10:45:00Z","revision":"R2"},"test":null,"resolution":{"status":"Open","resolved_at":null,"note":null},"confidence":null,"rests_on":[],"last_check":null,"role":null,"state":null,"common_reading":null,"angle":null,"mechanism":[],"w